# A second loop of mandatory actions, through a target rather than an Aura's choice of host (CR 104.4b, 732.4), and across
# owners. Bot2 Entombs its own Worldgorger Dragon on turn 2; on turn 5 Bot1 casts Necromancy at sorcery speed, and its
# enters ability targets the Dragon, the only creature card in any graveyard. The Dragon enters under Bot1's control (CR 110.2), and its enters ability, Bot1's, exiles all other permanents Bot1
# controls: Necromancy and three Swamps. Necromancy's leaves ability makes the Dragon's controller, Bot1, sacrifice it,
# and it goes to its owner's graveyard, Bot2's. The Dragon's leaves ability returns the exiled cards under their owner's
# control, Bot1's. Necromancy enters again and its enters ability must target a creature card in a graveyard: the
# Dragon in Bot2's graveyard is the only one, so it is chosen without asking (CR 603.3d), and round it goes. Nobody can
# do anything at any priority but pass or tap a land: both pass, and once the loop has come round three times the game is
# a draw (docs/rules-exceptions.md, RX-4).

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Necromancy
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp
Entomb
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island
Worldgorger Dragon
Island x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Entomb.Cast
Bot2.Search(Worldgorger Dragon)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Necromancy.Cast

[Expect]
Result = Draw
DrawReason = MandatoryLoop
Turn = 5
Step = Main1
Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Status = (absent)
Bot2.Status = (absent)
